# 02 — Case Design, Security Hand-Off & Stack-Neutral Test Levels (`Q4`, `Q5`, `Q8`–`Q11`)

<!-- GEN: Why: Most escaped defects and authorization bypasses live off the happy path, and choosing the wrong test level makes verification either blind to service rules or slow and brittle (`Q4`, `Q5`, `Q8`–`Q11`). Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, populate roles, scopes, and test runners for {{project_name}}. -->

## 1. Mandatory Coverage Categories (`Q4`, `Q9`, `Q10`)

Every feature test plan must cover all applicable categories below:

- [ ] **Happy Path**: Every approved BDD scenario and primary user/API flow.
- [ ] **Validation & Input Boundaries**: Equivalence classes, missing required fields, malformed payloads, and exact boundaries (`0`, `1`, `max`, `max + 1`, pagination edges).
- [ ] **Permission & Data-Scope Matrix (`Role × Environment × Action × Object`)**: Every mutating or restricted read operation tested across `{{roles}}` × `{{environments}}` × `{{data_scopes}}`, including direct API/service calls that must return `401`, `403`, or scoped `404` even when the UI hides the control.
- [ ] **`security-review` (`SR14`) Runtime Hand-Off Cases**: Every runtime-dependent `PLAUSIBLE` finding or authorization/rate-limit/concurrency check handed over from `security-review` converted into an explicit test case tagged `security-handoff:<SR-ID>`.
- [ ] **UI / Client State Matrix (when client surface exists)**: `loading` (no layout jump), `empty` (zero records vs zero filter matches), `error + retry`, and `populated`.
- [ ] **External Provider Failures & Timeouts**: Upstream timeout, `5xx`, and malformed responses for `{{external_providers}}` (stubbed at network boundary and labelled `stubbed`).
- [ ] **Idempotency & Concurrency**: Repeated submission, double-click/retry handling, and concurrent edits on shared records.
- [ ] **Out-of-Scope Guards (`Q9`)**: Explicit checks proving capabilities listed under brief "scope out" are not exposed or executable.
- [ ] **Targeted Regression Set (`Q10`)**: Existing flows sharing `{{regression_areas}}` (tables, contracts, shared components, or permission guards).

