## 2. Case Format & Concrete Expected Results (`Q8`, `Q11`)

Every case uses the standard structure below and grades impact with **`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`; never use legacy numbered priorities):

```text
<TC-ID>  [traces: <AC-ID> | security-handoff:<SR-ID> | out-of-scope-guard | regression]   risk: <BLOCKER | MAJOR | MINOR>   level: <api | ui | visual | integration | manual>
Given:   <deterministic seed data, actor role, tenant/owner scope, and initial state>
When:    <exact user interaction or API/service request>
Then:    <concrete observable outcome: HTTP/RPC status, response fields, DB state, event, or UI state/message>
Target:  <environment, route/endpoint/screen, Role × Scope>
```

### Risk Tier Ordering (`Q8`)
1. **`BLOCKER` (Run First)**: Core happy-path AC, `Role × Environment × Action × Object` permission and cross-tenant isolation checks, `security-review` (`SR14`) runtime checks, and data/financial integrity cases.
2. **`MAJOR` (Run Second)**: Input validation, boundary values, UI state matrix (`loading`, `empty`, `error`, `populated`), external failure handling, out-of-scope guards (`Q9`), and regressions (`Q10`).
3. **`MINOR` (Run Last)**: Secondary cosmetic details and non-destructive edge formatting.

---

## 3. Selecting the Cheapest Proving Test Level (`Q5`)

Assign each test case to the lowest, fastest stack-neutral boundary that proves the requirement:

| Test Level | Proves in `{{project_name}}` | Workspace Runner / Tooling | Owner | Selection Rule |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Unit** | Pure domain/state logic in isolation | `{{unit_tool}}` | {{unit_owner}} | Enforced via prerequisite CLI gate; not planned case-by-case in QA test plan |
| **Integration** | Repository queries, DB constraints, transactions, scope filtering | `{{integration_tool}}` | {{integration_owner}} | Use when persistence invariants or query scoping cannot be observed through the API |
| **API / Service Acceptance** | Real service requests with per-role auth, status codes, payload contract, persisted records, side effects, `Role × Scope` matrix | `{{api_tool}}` | {{api_owner}} | Default level for business rules, permission denials (`401`/`403`/`404`), concurrency, and `SR14` hand-offs |
| **UI / Client End-to-End** | Rendered user flows, navigation, forms, 4 UI states, role-driven visibility, runtime console/network health | `{{ui_tool}}` | {{ui_owner}} | Use for end-to-end user journeys and client state transitions; do not duplicate combinatorial API matrix here |
| **Visual Fidelity** | Layout, responsive viewports, and visual states against approved design | `{{visual_tool}}` | {{visual_owner}} | Use when feature has an approved visual design or UI mockup |
| **Manual** | Non-automatable physical/external flows | Step-by-step protocol + evidence capture | {{manual_owner}} | Permitted **only** with a written justification in the plan |

